          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Magic Squares in History and Culture"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.121,
            0.769,
            0.177
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The first magic square ever recorded, the Lo Shu Square, dates back over 2000 years to ancient China. The legend tells of a catastrophic flood on the Lo River, during which the gods sent"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.243,
            0.176,
            0.769,
            0.231
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "a turtle to save the people. The turtle carried a "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "3 \\times 3"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " grid on its back, with the numbers 1 to 9 arranged in a magical pattern."
            }
          ],
          "continues_prev": true
        },
        {
